equests":["Q3","Q6","Q4"],"summary":"The absenteeism story is a measurement artifact. ShiftLine began recording partial-day absences, which the legacy process did not count. Full-day absences rose only 1.1%, and the independent dispatch log shows no change in trips missed for lack of an operator or in late pull-outs. On-time performance fell on routes where recovery time was cut (Groups A and B), with the largest drop on the construction corridors. The 17 routes with no recovery cut and no construction stayed flat. This separation supports recovery cuts and construction as real causes and argues against a systemwide measurement artifact. Preferred actions: restore recovery time, set construction running times, and restate the absence data. Discipline based on ShiftLine counts would punish operators for a recording change."}}